Below is a summary of what’s happening, followed by two small *SEARCH/REPLACE* style patches—one in the React wrapper (to turn on the “light” style by default), and one in the core SASS file (to bump up the border and divider colors to meet 3:1). 

1) Bug summary and root cause  
- In the default (“dark”) variant the *un-selected* tabs use a very light grey background (`#f4f4f4`) plus a very light grey border (`#e0e0e0`), which only yields about a 1.1:1 non-text contrast against the surrounding area.  
- WCAG 1.4.11 requires a **minimum 3:1 contrast** for “visual information required to identify UI components.”  
- The fix is simply to ensure the un-selected tabs (and their internal dividers) use a darker border (or background) that meets 3:1.  

2) Patches  

——————————————————————————————  
